#### Overview

## How do you make a seat with a CEO worth competing for?

Melo Portal is the membership app of Project Melo, a community that connects students with like-minded peers and CEOs. Members earn tokens and bid them on events. I designed the portal in a team of four.

#### Research

## We started by asking half the community.

Before designing anything, I interviewed 89 members, half of everyone in Melo. Two questions came out of it and shaped the whole portal:

> How do we make bidding exciting the moment an event opens?
>
> How do we make members feel the prestige of belonging?

So I spent the time on the two experiences that answer them:

{% points %}
{% point title="Bidding" text="Make competing for a seat quick and a little thrilling." /%}

{% point title="Membership card and tokens" text="Make belonging feel premium." /%}
{% /points %}

![](/images/experience/project-melo/image.webp)

![](/images/experience/project-melo/image-1.webp)

#### Bidding

## Slide to bid beat every other input.

I iterated through a number pad, a counter, a plain input field and more before settling on slide to bid. It lowers the effort of bidding, and it does three things the others could not:

{% points %}
{% point title="See what is left" text="The slider shows the share of all tokens remaining." /%}

{% point title="See the floor" text="The minimum bid is visible at a glance." /%}

{% point title="Barely type" text="One gesture is the whole input." /%}
{% /points %}

![](/images/experience/project-melo/image-2.webp)

#### Membership card

## The card is the membership.

Vertical cards were the trend, so I iterated on a vertical design and invited members to give feedback on each version. Dark blue and orange carry the core Melo brand and give members an identity that feels premium.

![](/images/experience/project-melo/image-3.webp)

Membership card iterations.

![](/images/experience/project-melo/image-4.webp)

The token claim flow and the final membership card.

#### Outcome

## Conversion rose 340% after launch.

Members praised the portal for how easy it was to use and how it looked.

